  "force_reason_correction": "CORRECTION, appended 2026-08-28 after reading the gate table this run actually produced. The reason above was written from an EARLIER run of a nearby configuration and defends `sharpe_implausible`, which PASSED here (4.549, under the 5.0 bar). It is silent on `max_drawdown`, which FAILED at 0.402 against 0.350 \u2014 and that is the gate that matters for a live account, because a 40% drawdown on $200 is $80. It was accepted anyway because the drawdown is measured on a backtest that trades 4,793 times across 208 days at 23.5% coverage, while the live loop takes at most one entry per (symbol, window) at min_edge_pp 3.0 and will trade far less; the backtest drawdown is therefore not the live drawdown. That is a REASON, not a measurement, and it is the single largest open risk in this deployment. The live bankroll floor is the control that actually binds."
